{
 "_about": "Bit timing for a bitrate and sample point: total TQ (at least minTq) = 1 + TSEG1 + TSEG2 = clock / (BRP * bitrate), sample point = (1 + TSEG1) / TQ. Among BRPs giving the bitrate exactly and TSEG1 placing the sample point at floor or ceil of samplePoint * TQ (within limits), the best has the smallest sample-point error, then TQ closest to preferredTq, then the smaller BRP, then the later sample point. SJW = min(TSEG2, sjw limit). expect null: no BRP gives the bitrate exactly. btr: SJA1000 BTR0/BTR1 (BTR0 = (SJW-1)<<6 | (BRP-1), BTR1 = (TSEG2-1)<<4 | (TSEG1-1), one sample).",
 "limits": {
  "fdNominal": {
   "brp": [
    1,
    1024
   ],
   "tseg1": [
    1,
    256
   ],
   "tseg2": [
    1,
    128
   ],
   "sjw": 128,
   "minTq": 8
  },
  "fdData": {
